<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African Q3 GDP up annualised 3.2 percent.</title>
<headline>S.African Q3 GDP up annualised 3.2 percent.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African gross domestic product (GDP) rose a seasonally adjusted and annualised 3.2 percent in the third quarter of 1996, the Central Statistical Service said.</p>
<p>It said second quarter GDP rose a revised 3.7 percent after a preliminary 3.5 percent estimated rise.</p>
<p>The figures are at constant 1990 market prices.</p>
<p>A Reuters poll of economists forecast a third quarter rise of 2.5 percent, with ideas ranging widely from 1.0 to 3.5 percent.  </p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted and annualised percentage change:</p>
<p>    At market prices:  Q3'96 (prel)   Q2'96 (rev)   Q1'96</p>
<p>     GDP		    3.2	     3.7	     3.3</p>
<p>At factor incomes:</p>
<p>     Total		  3.0	     3.9	     3.1</p>
<p>     Agriculture	  54.6	    52.2	   82.5</p>
<p>     Non-Agricultural    0.5	    1.8	     0.4</p>
<p>     Mining		 -7.0	   -5.0	    -0.1</p>
<p>     Secondary industry  0.5	    2.0	     0.5</p>
<p>     Manufacturing	-0.5	    1.5	    -0.7</p>
<p>     Tertiary industry   1.8	    2.9	     0.4</p>
<p>	  -- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
